From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:18:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 511/511] [DS4.1] SP prefill MoE: the combine writes the
 exchange slots and the exchange runs under it

Each sequence-parallel layer's MoE combine (the shared expert folded in) wrote
its whole output, then the runner's reduce-scatter hook copied every rank's
block into the exchange's send and parts slots: 157 MB a layer at a
15,395-token prompt, 80 copies of 39.4 MB at 345 us each, 1.29% of the
prefill step (request inventory 5, TP4 ring, rank 0). The exchange then ran
with nothing beside it: 7.74% of the step.

When the model's hook is installed, the runner asks the TileLang experts to
defer their folded combine: apply launches the dispatch, the cast, both
GEMMs and the SwiGLU, and keeps the combine as combine(start, stop, out).
The hook's writer is that combine, so each block goes straight into its slot,
one launch a block and slice; a token's sum reads only its own routes, so
every row keeps its bits. The pad rows are still TileLang's zeros. The copy
writer is gone: the hook requires the deferred combine.

Block by block, _project_exchange writes the other ranks' blocks of a slice,
starts that slice's exchange on the side stream, then writes this rank's own
block under it. The MoE output is exchanged in moe_slices(T) slices, one a
4,096 tokens (three at the 15K prompt and at the TP4 recipe's 16,288-token
long-prefill chunk, four at a full 16,384-row step), so the combine after the
first slice's other blocks runs beside the exchange. WO's two
slices take the same order: each exchange starts a block earlier. The same
rows land in the same slots and the exchange only moves them, so the parts
are bit for bit the old ones.

Ceilings (the fusion survey, same traces): the copies 1.31% of the prefill,
the exchange under the combine and the copies 6.32%.

Tests: the deferred combine, piece by piece into separate buffers, equals the
one combine for the BF16, FP32 and folded kernels, a callable shared addend
called once by run; the hook with the real combine sends each other rank's
block and keeps this rank's with the copies' bits, pad rows from TileLang's
fill, at one to twelve slices; each slice is exchanged after the other ranks'
blocks of it and before this rank's own (the generic writer too); the runner
defers only a folded combine bound for the hook, hands it over and resets the
experts' state; the experts defer only a folded combine.
benchmark_deepseek_v41_moe_exchange.py times the combine into the slots
against the combine and copies (the exchange stubbed), gated, at TP4 and TP3.
